    "description": "Tree farm, level 1 of 3: shell and fittings (what soldiers build first). Over budget: 344 blocks vs 102 (the lumber camp brief; the tree farm has no budget of its own), first build 268 vs 200; 19 x 14 instead of 11 x 11 because the yard moved outside the plot. The lumber camp's tier-6 upgrade: a fenced planting plot (11 x 13, spruce fence on capped cobblestone piers, a timber gateway) holding only three raised dirt rows and lanes, saplings 3 apart with open sky above; beside it, outside the fence, the woodcutter's yard: a 5 x 4 gabled shed in the sawmill's look (oak door; chest, grindstone workstation, barrel), a log pile, chopping block, composter, cobblestone slab paths. L1: plot with empty rows, shed, yard. L2: oak, birch and spruce saplings in the rows, a lychgate roof with lanterns, lanterns on the piers, shutters, a sawhorse, a cauldron and barrel by the gate. L3: a lean-to drying shed over the logs, a hanging sign (the Studio does not draw hanging signs), banners by the shed door, potted saplings on a shelf, flowers along the outside of the fence, moss, an axe in the block.",
    "changes": "Quality-check fix: the L3 drying lean-to's high back edge floated (posts only at the front); spruce fence posts now stand on the log pile under it. Nothing else changed from v3.",
